From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:15:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Handle dogmatic and vacuous opinions in belief fusion

Cumulative and averaging belief fusion divided by the uncertainty of
each source (u_a / u_i), so a single dogmatic source (u = 0) turned
the result into NaN. Averaging fusion of only vacuous opinions also
produced a NaN base rate (0 / 0).

* Compute the product of the other sources' uncertainties directly
  instead of dividing by u_i.
* If any source is dogmatic, return the average of the dogmatic
  sources, the limit of both fusion operators for equally dogmatic
  sources.
* If all sources are vacuous, return the vacuous opinion with the
  average base rate (cumulative fusion previously returned the first
  opinion's base rate).
* Compute the fused base rate from the certainty weights
  (1 - u_i) * prod_{j != i} u_j directly, avoiding cancellation for
  nearly vacuous sources. The result is unchanged otherwise.
* Divide the averaging fusion uncertainty by the sum of the weights.
  The missing division was masked so far, as updateUncertainty()
  replaces an inconsistent uncertainty by 1 - sum(b).
